Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Well, in C, you would write an if statement like this:

if (condition) {

... do something...

}

If the condition is true, the code inside the if block will be executed.  If the condition is false, the code inside the else block will be executed.  Here’s an example of an if statement in C:

if (x == 5) {
printf("x is 5");
} else {
printf("x is not 5");
}

This will print "x is 5" if x equals 5, and "x is not 5" if x does not equal 5.
